Still, items usually available only in the end game greatly improve the  
early game, even for a player who isn't familiar with them.
My first ascension was done with the help of an early wish (Orb of Fate,  
being a monk the usual DSM was not so useful). And I don't think I would  
have managed it so easily without it (I was never able to reach the quest  
before that). After that, I managed to reach the mid-game on a much more  
regular basis. Maybe it was just a coincidence.
Of course, that doesn't mean that an early wish is a guarantee to reach a  
more advanced stage of the game. I think it let you think about some other  
things that basic move-to-move survival. Maybe it's "bad" because then you  
won't learn the required skills to survive in a normal situation, but it  
can also let you develop other aspects of the game.

